\ Spitfire: the mission's briefing, between choosing a mission and flying
\ it. A map of the area from above: the coastlines and the lochs' shores,
\ the airfields and towns within it, the Spitfire's start and its heading,
\ the raid's start, track and target, the mission's target, a scale bar in
\ miles and the north mark; the map's square takes in every point the
\ mission names, with a margin, and at least 30 km across. Beside it the
\ particulars, read from the mission: the time of day and the moon, the
\ aircraft and its guns or cameras, the propeller, the boost, the start,
\ the weather and the opposition. Below them the mission's own briefing.

16 constant map-left
32 constant map-top
288 constant map-size
332 constant particulars-left
410 constant values-left
214 constant values-width
332 constant briefing-top
0xff6040 constant raid-colour
0xffe080 constant heading-colour

\ a text broken at spaces into lines no wider than a width in pixels
: wrapped-lines ( text width -- lines )
	| text width |
	[ ] to lines
	"" to filling
	text " +" split to words
	0 words size 1 do k
		words k @i to word
		filling "" = if word else filling " " + word + then to candidate
		candidate text-width width > filling "" = not and if
			lines filling add-last! drop
			word to filling
		else
			candidate to filling
		then
	loop
	lines filling add-last! ;

\ metres as feet, to the nearest hundred
: hundreds-of-feet ( metres -- feet ) 3.28084 * 100 / round 100 * ;

\ the places marked on the map when they fall within it, each [ landmark name ]
: map-places ( -- places )
	[ [ :turnhouse "TURNHOUSE" ] [ :drem "DREM" ] [ :abbotsinch "ABBOTSINCH" ] [ :dalcross "DALCROSS" ]
	  [ :acklington "ACKLINGTON" ] [ :wick "WICK" ] [ :vaernes "VAERNES" ]
	  [ :edinburgh-castle "EDINBURGH" ] [ :glasgow-cathedral "GLASGOW" ] [ :greenock "GREENOCK" ]
	  [ :clydebank "CLYDEBANK" ] [ :tynemouth "TYNEMOUTH" ] [ :nidaros "TRONDHEIM" ]
	  [ :forth-bridge "FORTH BRIDGE" ] [ :farne-islands "FARNE ISLANDS" ] [ :inverness-castle "INVERNESS" ] ] ;

\ the ground points a mission names, each [ x z ]: the start, the raid's start and target, the mission's target, the tug's start
: mission-points ( mission -- points )
	| mission |
	mission@start first to start
	[ [ start first start 2 @i ] ] to points
	mission@raid to plan
	plan null? not if
		points [ plan@start first plan@start 2 @i ] add-last! drop
		points [ plan@target first plan@target 2 @i ] add-last! drop
	then
	mission :target null @or to target
	target null? not if
		target landmark-ground to place
		points [ place first place 2 @i ] add-last! drop
	then
	mission :tug-start null @or to tug-place
	tug-place null? not if points [ tug-place first tug-place 2 @i ] add-last! drop then
	points ;

\ the map's centre, metres east and north, and its scale, pixels a metre: the square round the mission's points with a 30% margin, at least 30 km across
: map-frame ( mission -- frame )
	| mission |
	mission mission-points to points
	points ( point | point first ) map to xs
	points ( point | point second ) map to zs
	xs 1e12 ' min2 reduce to west
	xs -1e12 ' max2 reduce to east
	zs 1e12 ' min2 reduce to south
	zs -1e12 ' max2 reduce to north
	east west - north south - max2 2 / 1.3 * 15000 max2 to half-size
	{ :x west east + 2 / :z south north + 2 / :scale map-size 2 / half-size / } ;

\ a ground point's place on the map, [ column row ]
: map-at ( frame x z -- column row )
	| frame x z |
	map-left map-size 2 / + x frame@x - frame@scale * +
	map-top map-size 2 / + z frame@z - frame@scale * - ;

\ whether a map place lies within the map's square, a margin inside it
: on-map? ( column row margin -- flag )
	| column row margin |
	column map-left margin + >= column map-left map-size + margin - <= and
	row map-top margin + >= and row map-top map-size + margin - <= and ;

\ the shore lines as map segments, each [ x0 y0 x1 y1 ]: the coastlines, Norway's shores and the lochs', each point kept 1.5 pixels or more from the last, a segment kept when an end lies within 50 pixels of the map
: map-lines ( frame -- segments )
	| frame |
	lochs keys ( key | lochs key @ :shores @ ) map [ ] ' concat reduce to loch-shores
	coastlines norway-shores concat loch-shores concat to shores
	[ ] to segments
	0 shores size 1 do k
		shores k @i to shore
		shore first spread frame -rot map-at to last-row to last-column
		1 shore size 1 do m
			shore m @i spread frame -rot map-at to row to column
			column last-column - sq row last-row - sq + 2.25 >= m shore size 1- = or if
				column row -50 on-map? last-column last-row -50 on-map? or if
					segments [ last-column last-row column row ] add-last! drop
				then
				column to last-column
				row to last-row
			then
		loop
	loop
	segments ;

\ the names already on the map, each the box it covers, [ left top right bottom ]
variable placed-labels
[ ] to placed-labels

\ whether a box overlaps any name already on the map
: label-clashes? ( left top right bottom -- flag )
	| left top right bottom |
	placed-labels ( box |
		left box 2 @i < right box first > and top box 3 @i < and bottom box second > and
	) filter size 0 > ;

\ where a mark's name goes: right of the mark, or left of it when the right side runs off the map or onto another name; null when both sides clash and the name may be left out, the right side when it may not
: place-label ( column row name gap required -- position )
	| column row name gap required ^placed-labels |
	name text-width to width
	row 6 - to top
	column gap + to right-left
	column gap - width - to left-left
	right-left width + map-left map-size + 2 - <= right-left top right-left width + top 12 + label-clashes? not and if
		right-left to left
	else left-left map-left 2 + >= left-left top left-left width + top 12 + label-clashes? not and if
		left-left to left
	else required if
		right-left width + map-left map-size + 2 - <= if right-left else left-left then to left
	else
		null exit
	then then then
	placed-labels [ left top left width + top 12 + ] add-last! drop
	[ left top ] ;

\ a mark on the map with its name beside it, when within the map; a place whose name has no room is left out
: draw-map-mark ( column row name colour required -- )
	| column row name colour required |
	column row 4 on-map? not if exit then
	column row name 5 required place-label to position
	position null? if exit then
	column 1 - row 1 - 3 3 colour fill-span
	position spread name colour draw-text ;

\ a cross on the map with its name beside it, when within the map
: draw-map-cross ( column row name colour -- )
	| column row name colour |
	column row 6 on-map? not if exit then
	column 4 - row 4 - column 4 + row 4 + colour draw-segment
	column 4 - row 4 + column 4 + row 4 - colour draw-segment
	column row name 7 true place-label spread name colour draw-text ;

\ the scale bar: the longest of 1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 50 and 100 miles no longer than 90 pixels, under the map's lower left corner
: draw-scale-bar ( frame -- )
	| frame |
	[ 1 2 5 10 20 50 100 ] ( miles | miles 1609.34 * frame@scale * 90 <= ) filter to fitting
	fitting size 0 = if exit then
	fitting last to miles
	miles 1609.34 * frame@scale * to length
	map-left 8 + to x
	map-top map-size + 10 - to y
	x y x length + y dial-ink draw-segment
	x y 3 - x y 3 + dial-ink draw-segment
	x length + y 3 - x length + y 3 + dial-ink draw-segment
	x length + 6 + y 6 - miles 1 = if "1 MILE" else miles "{0} MILES" format then dial-ink draw-text ;

\ the map: its square, the shores, the places, the raid's track, the target, the start and its heading, the scale and north; whatever of the shores falls outside covered over by the screen's ground
: draw-briefing-map ( mission frame segments -- )
	| mission frame segments ^placed-labels |
	map-left map-top map-size map-size board-colour fill-span
	dial-ink 0.55 dimmed to shore-colour
	segments ( segment | segment spread shore-colour draw-segment ) each
	0 0 640 map-top wall-colour fill-span
	0 map-top map-size + 640 480 map-top - map-size - wall-colour fill-span
	0 map-top map-left map-size wall-colour fill-span
	map-left map-size + map-top 640 map-left - map-size - map-size wall-colour fill-span
	map-left map-top map-size map-size edge-colour outline
	[ ] to placed-labels
	mission@start first to start
	frame start first start 2 @i map-at to start-row to start-column
	mission@start second PI 180 / * to bearing
	start-column start-row start-column bearing sin 14 * + start-row bearing cos 14 * - heading-colour draw-segment
	start-column start-row 3 heading-colour fill-disc
	mission@raid to plan
	plan null? not if
		frame plan@start first plan@start 2 @i map-at to raid-row to raid-column
		frame plan@target first plan@target 2 @i map-at to target-row to target-column
		raid-column raid-row target-column target-row raid-colour draw-segment
		target-column target-row "TARGET" raid-colour draw-map-cross
		raid-column raid-row "RAID" raid-colour true draw-map-mark
	then
	mission :aircraft :fighter @or :reconnaissance = if
		mission@target landmark-ground to place
		frame place first place 2 @i map-at "TIRPITZ" raid-colour draw-map-cross
	then
	mission :tug-start null @or to tug-place
	tug-place null? not if frame tug-place first tug-place 2 @i map-at "TUG" dial-ink true draw-map-mark then
	start-column start-row "YOU" 6 true place-label spread "YOU" heading-colour draw-text
	dial-ink 0.8 dimmed to place-colour
	map-places ( place |
		place first landmark-ground to point
		frame point first point 2 @i map-at place second place-colour false draw-map-mark
	) each
	frame draw-scale-bar
	map-left map-size + 16 - map-top 6 + "N" dial-ink draw-text
	map-left map-size + 12 - map-top 20 + map-left map-size + 12 - map-top 30 + dial-ink draw-segment ;

\ whether a mission may be flown in the Hurricane: every armed mission but the flying lesson, which is the two-seat Spitfire's
: aircraft-choosable? ( mission -- flag )
	| mission |
	mission :aircraft :fighter @or :reconnaissance = if false exit then
	mission :lesson false @or mission :air-firing false @or not and not ;

\ how many of a type, by the name the briefing gives it
: kind-plural ( kind -- text )
	| kind |
	kind :ju-88 = if "JU 88s" exit then
	kind :he-111 = if "HE 111s" exit then
	"BF 110s" ;

\ the particulars, each [ label value ], read from the mission and the aircraft chosen for it
: briefing-particulars ( mission choice -- rows )
	| mission choice |
	mission :moon null @or to moon
	mission@night if
		moon null? if "NIGHT, NO MOON" else moon second "NIGHT, THE MOON {0:.0f} DEG UP" format then
	else
		"DAY"
	then to time-text
	mission :aircraft :fighter @or :reconnaissance = if
		"SPITFIRE PR, UNARMED, SPLIT CAMERAS"
	else choice :hurricane = mission aircraft-choosable? and if
		"HURRICANE MK I, EIGHT BROWNINGS, 334 OR 287 ROUNDS EACH"
	else
		"SPITFIRE MK I, EIGHT BROWNINGS, 300 ROUNDS EACH"
	then then to aircraft-text
	mission@propeller :two-pitch = if "TWO-PITCH" else "CONSTANT-SPEED" then to propeller-text
	mission@emergency if "+6 LB, +12 LB EMERGENCY ON 100 OCTANE" else "+6 LB, 87 OCTANE" then to boost-text
	mission@start to start
	start 3 @i if
		"ON THE RUNWAY"
	else
		start 2 @i 2.23694 * start first second hundreds-of-feet "AIRBORNE, {0} FT, {1:.0f} MPH" format
	then to start-text
	mission@visibility clear-visibility >= if "CLEAR" else mission@visibility 1609.34 / "VISIBILITY {0:.1f} MILES" format then to visibility-text
	mission@cover 0 = if
		visibility-text ", NO CLOUD" +
	else
		mission@base hundreds-of-feet mission@cover 10 * round visibility-text "{0}, CUMULUS {1}/10 AT {2} FT" format
	then to weather-text
	mission@raid to plan
	plan null? if
		mission :aircraft :fighter @or :reconnaissance = if "HEAVY AND LIGHT FLAK ROUND THE FJORD"
		else mission :air-firing false @or if "NONE: A LYSANDER TUG AND ITS DROGUE"
		else "NONE" then then
	else
		plan@height hundreds-of-feet plan@kind kind-plural plan@n-vics 3 * "{0} {1} AT {2} FT" format
		mission :escort [ ] @or size to n-escort
		n-escort 0 > if n-escort ", {0} BF 110s ESCORTING" format + then
	then to opposition-text
	[ [ "TIME" time-text ] [ "AIRCRAFT" aircraft-text ] [ "PROPELLER" propeller-text ] [ "BOOST" boost-text ]
	  [ "START" start-text ] [ "WEATHER" weather-text ] [ "ENEMY" opposition-text ] ] to rows
	mission :wingmen [ ] @or size to n-wingmen
	n-wingmen 0 > if rows [ "SQUADRON" n-wingmen "{0} MORE SPITFIRES WITH YOU" format ] add-last! drop then
	rows ;

\ the briefing screen: the mission's name, the map, the particulars, the briefing, and what the keys do, the choice of aircraft among them where the mission allows it
: draw-briefing ( mission frame segments choice -- )
	| mission frame segments choice |
	0 0 640 480 wall-colour fill-span
	320 12 mission@name 0xffffff centred-print
	mission frame segments draw-briefing-map
	map-top 4 + to y
	mission choice briefing-particulars to rows
	0 rows size 1 do k
		rows k @i to row
		particulars-left y row first heading-colour draw-text
		row second values-width wrapped-lines to value-lines
		0 value-lines size 1 do m
			values-left y value-lines m @i dial-ink draw-text
			y 13 + to y
		loop
		y 4 + to y
	loop
	mission :briefing "" @or 640 32 - wrapped-lines to lines
	0 lines size 1 do k
		16 briefing-top k 13 * + lines k @i dial-ink draw-text
	loop
	mission aircraft-choosable? if
		320 448 "LEFT AND RIGHT: SPITFIRE OR HURRICANE" heading-colour centred-print
	then
	320 462 "RETURN OR START FLIES  -  ESCAPE FOR THE MISSIONS" 0xffffff centred-print ;
